{
  "program": "COUSR01C",
  "caseId": "case14",
  "description": "The ENTER half of the ENTER-versus-REENTER pair. CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT arrives as 0, so NOT CDEMO-PGM-REENTER at app/cbl/COUSR01C.cbl:83 is true: the program flips the context to re-enter at :84, moves LOW-VALUES over the whole output map at :85, places the cursor at :86 and paints at :87. Nothing is validated, nothing is read from the five data fields and USRSEC is not touched - which is why no AID is declared here, since EIBAID is not evaluated on this path and declaring one would imply the key mattered. Two consequences of :85 are pinned. The MOVE blanks the header too, but SEND-USRADD-SCREEN immediately repopulates the six header fields and ERRMSGO, so only the five DATA fields are still LOW-VALUES when the map goes out - x'00' at each declared width, which is a different observable from the spaces INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS writes on the PF4 path. And the returned CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT is 1, so the next call takes the other branch: the context flip travels in the payload, not in a session.",
